{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKQ5wETEgoBmsijKaMp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, they still work. According to this project's Ludion lesson notes, wrangler 4.117.0 and later renamed the test endpoints from `/cdn-cgi/handler/*` (for example `/cdn-cgi/handler/scheduled`) to `/cdn-cgi/local/*` (for example `/cdn-cgi/local/scheduled`). `wrangler dev` and the Vite plugin quietly rewrite the old paths to the new ones, so existing scripts and curl commands keep working without errors. You have wrangler 4.148.0, so the new paths are the standard ones, and it's worth updating to them so you don't depend on the rewrite. I couldn't confirm that this change came with a Miniflare v5 move: the notes only tie it to the wrangler version, and I didn't check the changelog."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8609,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8609},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15e0f100-e720-499f-a553-f8da2e5f86f7","uuid":"9c2c3fa3-b723-4399-9933-b1b2f4c4b177","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:48:16.551Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKQ5f6wNp1kMUtpQ2Ym"}
